================================================================================
ADDITIONAL LIABILITY DISCLAIMER FOR SECURITY-ASSESSMENT TOOLING
================================================================================

This repository bundles security-assessment frameworks (blueteam / redteam /
greenteam / yellowteam) that automate scanning, threat modeling, exploit
prototyping, and remediation suggestions. They are provided for the use of
software teams reviewing their own systems with appropriate authorization.

You assume full responsibility for:

  1. Lawful, authorized use. Running offensive components (redteam, exploit
     prototypes, recon tooling) against systems you do not own or do not have
     explicit written authorization to test is illegal in many jurisdictions.
     The authors of this harness bear no responsibility for misuse.

  2. Correctness of findings and fixes. The harness combines AI-driven and
     deterministic analysis. Both can produce false positives, miss real
     issues, propose fixes that introduce new vulnerabilities, or generate
     code that does not match your security policy. Every finding and every
     proposed fix MUST be independently reviewed by a qualified human before
     being acted on.

  3. Operational outcomes. The harness may invoke external scanners and APIs
     (semgrep, OSV, npm audit, secretlint, ZAP, LLM providers, etc.), modify
     your repository (writing reports, generating code), or shell out to
     subprocesses. Outages, data loss, regressions, or contractual / regulatory
     exposure resulting from running this software are entirely the user's
     responsibility.

  4. Compliance and disclosure. Nothing in this software constitutes legal
     advice, a compliance attestation (OWASP ASVS, CAS, PCI, HIPAA, FOIP,
     etc.), or a binding security certification. Outputs are tooling artifacts
     and must be reviewed in the context of your specific control framework.

By using this software you acknowledge the above and agree that the authors,
copyright holders, and contributors are not liable for any direct, indirect,
incidental, consequential, special, punitive, or exemplary damages arising
from its use.
